@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Shipment Details presentation — FRO-316
+
+Controlled, unconnected React presentation for the redesigned Shipment Details page. This is preparation: the live route (`src/routes/secured/shipments/$shipmentId.tsx`) and `shipment-detail.tsx` are unchanged. No service, GraphQL document, wire model, authority, persistence or live operation is delivered here.
+
+**Terms:** Order = purchase order = stock-list item. Colli = a permanently identified handling unit. Individual colli = a participating colli outside every load unit. Transport pieces = load units + individual collis.
+
+## Composition and data ownership
+
+- `ShipmentDetailsPreparedPage` composes the TopBar title **Shipment · [number]** and the tabs **Overview · Orders and collis · History & activity · Documents · Available actions**. The route owns `?tab=` and passes `tab`/`onTabChange`. Arrow/Home/End keys are handled by a local wrapper; the shared `Tabs` primitive is unchanged.
+- Drafts (route, purpose, both Notes, comment, cancellation and location reasons) live in the page above the tab panels, because `TabPanel` unmounts inactive panels. They reset when the Shipment number changes. Packing and participation drafts live in their modals while open.
+- `shipment-details-types.ts` holds UI view models. They are **not** wire contracts. The caller resolves `capabilities` from authority and state; hidden controls are not authorization, and the server rechecks every command.
+- Commands return `OperationResult`. A failure keeps the draft and shows the supplied message; `reconciliation` items open the delivery-note step.
+- `slots.documents`, `slots.deliveryNotes` and `slots.arrivalForm` take the existing `AttachmentPanel`, `DeliveryNotesCard` and arrival/handover form unchanged.
+- Components: `shipment-status-card` (pill, display-only steps, exception alert, blockers, Dispatch confirmation), `shipment-route-cards` (Shipment details, Shipment purpose, Final handover), `shipment-notes-card`, `shipment-orders-tab` (Purchase orders, Shipment packages, participation editor), `shipment-packing-modal` (Optional repacking and Review repacking), `shipment-history-tab`, `shipment-actions-tab`, `shipment-change-dialogs` (Ready warning, delivery-note reconciliation). Pure rules are in `shipment-details-values.ts`.
+- Labels: `localization/shipment-details-labels.ts` (EN/EL). Terms the composer already uses take their Greek from production labels; the geography labels match `release/0.0.2` (FRO-339). The remaining Greek strings are proposed for office review.
+
+## Required controller and contract work
+
+| Owner   | Must supply                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |
+| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| FRO-325 | READY_FOR_DISPATCH; packing read/save; readiness confirmation; document assign/replace/clear; dispatch from Ready with the saved number; cancellation from both pre-dispatch states; participation read with Order display data (owner reference, client, vessel, supplier, root Order number); readiness and dispatch blocker lists with stable codes (messages are localized by the controller); load-unit label/weight rules; omitted net weight and notes preserved |
+| FRO-344 | Route, purpose/destination and participation editing; readiness invalidation; mode-change document resolution; delivery-note reconciliation items and the resolution command                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
+| FRO-339 | Geography reads and validation (on `release/0.0.2`; `GetShipment` does not fetch geography yet)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
+| FRO-345 | Status history with event ids and full reasons, recorded operations, comments                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
+| FRO-292 | Internal/External Notes reads and updates                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| FRO-299 | Per-colli description, package type, dimensions, gross weight and their sources                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
+| FRO-324 | Historical-arrival flag, unknown facts, date-only precision, recording metadata                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
+| FRO-297 | `dangerousGoodsCount` (null shows Unavailable)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+
+Until these exist, keep the live page. Do not emulate them with broad updates, invented fields or fixtures.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- `Modal` has no accessible-name prop; the dialogs show their title visually but are not programmatically named. Adding one belongs to the shared primitive (the FRO-326 branch proposes `Modal.ariaLabel`).
+- Country, city and warehouse pickers use `Select`; switch to `Combobox` if the option lists grow long.
+- Event titles for historical arrivals use the generic "Created — Arrived" wording unless the controller supplies a summary.
+
+## Local review
+
+Run `npm run dev` in this client, then open `http://127.0.0.1:3000/dev/fro316/index.html`. The page renders only in Vite dev mode on loopback and is not imported by the application or included in the production build. It uses fictional demo data and simulated effects: no API requests, and a refresh resets everything. Toolbar: 10 scenarios (also `?scenario=`), screen state (loading, empty, error), view-only access, and fail-next-save. Documents and delivery notes show placeholders for the existing production components.
+
+## Verification scope
+
+Tests cover value rules (steps, measurements, counts, packing validation, participation checks, material route changes), the Greek label set, status/exception presentation, edit gating and warnings, Notes independence, participation, packing review and confirmation, history, available actions, and the page (tab order, keys, drafts across tabs and language, View history, packing entry). They prove controlled presentation only, not backend permissions, concurrency or transactions.
